**Goal Model – Multi‑Robot Resource Delivery Mission**

---

## 1. Goal Tables  

| Name | Text | Runtime | Goal Type | Target Condition / Enquired Info | Relation | Justification |
|------|------|---------|-----------|----------------------------------|----------|---------------|
| **G1** | Deliver requested resources to the specified location | – | Achieve | *Resources are physically present at the destination and ready for use.* | – (root) | The mission’s ultimate objective is to have the requested items delivered to the user‑defined location. |
| **G2** | Collect resources from storage | # | Perform | – | AND (G4, G2.1) | Collection comprises a battery check **and** the actual collection steps; they may run in parallel (e.g., several robots collecting from different storages). |
| **G4** | Battery check during collection | FALLBACK(G4.1,G4.2) | Perform | – | AND (G4.1, G4.2) | If the battery is low, the mission must fall back to a re‑assignment strategy; otherwise normal collection proceeds. |
| **G4.1** | Battery sufficient during collection | – | Perform | – | – | Normal case – no special action required. |
| **G4.2** | Battery low during collection | – | Perform | – | – | Triggers re‑charge and re‑assignment tasks. |
| **G2.1** | Perform collection steps | ; | Perform | – | AND (AT1‑AT4) | The steps *navigate → request → wait → retrieve* must occur sequentially for each robot. |
| **G3** | Deliver resources to destination | # | Perform | – | AND (G5, G3.1) | Delivery also requires a battery check **and** the actual delivery steps; they can be executed in parallel. |
| **G5** | Battery check during delivery | FALLBACK(G5.1,G5.2) | Perform | – | AND (G5.1, G5.2) | Low battery during delivery forces a fallback to checkpoint‑return and re‑assignment. |
| **G5.1** | Battery sufficient during delivery | – | Perform | – | – | Normal delivery can proceed. |
| **G5.2** | Battery low during delivery | – | Perform | – | – | Triggers checkpoint return, re‑assignment, and failure‑handling tasks. |
| **G3.1** | Perform delivery steps | ; | Perform | – | AND (AT5‑AT6) | The steps *navigate → deliver* must occur sequentially. |
| **G6** | Failure handling when cannot return to checkpoint | – | Perform | – | AND (AT10, AT11) | If the robot cannot return to a checkpoint, an alert and report must be issued. |

