## 2. Task Tables  

| Name | Text | Relation | Location | Number of Robots | Justification |
|------|------|----------|----------|------------------|---------------|
| **AT1** | Navigate to storage location | AND (G2.1) | *storage* | 1 | One robot must physically reach the storage to start the collection. |
| **AT2** | Send request for resource | AND (G2.1) | *storage* | 1 | The robot must communicate the exact resource specification to the storage. |
| **AT3** | Wait for resource retrieval | AND (G2.1) | *storage* | 1 | The robot must idle until the storage confirms the resource is ready. |
| **AT4** | Retrieve resource | AND (G2.1) | *storage* | 1 | The robot physically picks up the resource. |
| **AT5** | Navigate to destination | AND (G3.1) | *destination* | 1 | One robot must travel to the user‑defined delivery location. |
| **AT6** | Deliver resource to destination | AND (G3.1) | *destination* | 1 | The robot places the resource at the destination. |
| **AT7** | Recharge battery | AND (G4.2) | *charging station* | 1 | When the battery is low during collection, the robot must recharge. |
| **AT8** | Assign mission to another robot | AND (G4.2, G5.2) | *control center* | 1 | After re‑charge or low‑battery during delivery, the current robot hands the task to a spare robot. |
| **AT9** | Return resource to checkpoint | AND (G5.2) | *checkpoint* | 1 | If battery is low during delivery, the robot must bring the resource back to a known safe point. |
| **AT10** | Trigger alert | AND (G6) | *control center* | 1 | Failure to return to checkpoint requires an immediate alert. |
| **AT11** | Send report to sector manager | AND (G6) | *control center* | 1 | The sector manager must be informed of the failure. |

